<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Why were people arguing?</h2>
      <p font-size="lg"><b>There was not one simple cause.</b></p>
      <grid padding-top="38pt" spacing="small" marker-straddle="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-shape="circle" marker-style="solid" marker-size="large" marker="icon">
        <grid-item colspan="15" cell-style="subtle">
          <grid-item-label><ai-icon query="tax paper and coins"></ai-icon></grid-item-label>
          <h4>Trade and taxes</h4>
          <p>People disputed economic rules, including taxes and trade.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15" cell-style="subtle">
          <grid-item-label><ai-icon query="regional map decision"></ai-icon></grid-item-label>
          <h4>Regional power</h4>
          <p>Leaders in Rio Grande do Sul wanted more say in decisions.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15" cell-style="subtle">
          <grid-item-label><ai-icon query="separate government building"></ai-icon></grid-item-label>
          <h4>Political future</h4>
          <p>Some rebels wanted a separate republic: a country with its own government.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="15" cell-style="subtle">
          <grid-item-label><ai-icon query="connected country regions"></ai-icon></grid-item-label>
          <h4>Imperial government</h4>
          <p>It wanted Brazil to remain together.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <p><b>Different people made different choices for different reasons.</b> No whole side was simply good or bad.</p>
      <p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://cultura.rs.gov.br/upload/arquivos/carga20210405/27100547-anais-ahrs-v-16-1.pdf">State Historical Archive of Rio Grande do Sul</a></p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>